      q: "Which of the following statements is/are TRUE for a group G?",
      options: ["If for all x, y ∈ G, (xy)^2 = x^2 y^2, then G is commutative.","If for all x ∈ G, x^2 = 1, then G is commutative (1 is the identity element of G).","If the order of G is 2, then G is commutative.","If G is commutative, then a subgroup of G need not be commutative."],
      answers: [0,1,2],
